==Battleground==
*1 [[Youcan]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*2 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 22 seconds<sup>660f</sup>.
*8 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*1 [[General GreGory]] spawns after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[General GreGory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The most important thing to consider about this stage is Youcan's [[Barrier]], which protects him from any attack that deals less than 266k damage, so either bring the [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast]] Cannon (even at level 1), or a [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]].

Offworld Weary's difficulty drops dramatically with more than one chapter's worth of [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] from [[Cats of the Cosmos]], so, if you struggle or don't want to risk wasting [[Cat Energy|energy]], get some/more of them before attempting this stage.

Bring units like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]] and [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] to debuff Youcan. For attackers, bring [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] and [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]]. If you have any [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Alien]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]], bring them. [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield Units]] can also help a lot. With all that, Youcan shouldn't be very hard to defeat. Once he is down, just kill the GreGories and Shibalien Elites and destroy the base.

''Note: DON'T bring [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] if your Anti-Starred Alien Treasures are only at or below 500%.''

==Trivia==
*Offworld Weary's Japanese name, Anata Tsukareteru no yo (あなた疲れてるのよ, "It is That You Are Tired") is a reference to "[https://dic.pixiv.net/a/モルダー、あなた疲れてるのよ Mulder, anata tsukareteru no yo]" (モルダー、あなた疲れてるのよ, "Mulder, it is that you are tired"), a supposed "famous quote" from [[wikipedia:TV Asahi|TV Asahi]]'s Japanese dub of ''[[wikipedia:The X-Files|The X-Files]]'' wherein [[wikipedia:Dana Scully|Dana Scully]] dismisses her partner [[wikipedia:Fox Mulder|Fox Mulder]]'s belief in paranormal phenomena by insisting that he has simply gone crazy from tiredness. The actual origin of the quote is unknown, as while similar lines are said in episodes 7 and 21 of season 1, this exact phrase is not in any official dub, giving it a similar status to ''[[wikipedia:Star Trek|Star Trek]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s "[[wikipedia:Beam me up, Scotty|Beam me, up Scotty]]".

